{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRyEfQszpGbNcV3YPnyQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The job ran every night; the script was failing and then dying before it could send the failure message. Both causes are in `ANSWER.md`, and the fixes are in the script and the plist. I tested the new script here with fake `claude` and `notify.sh`, but haven't run it on your Mac.\n\n**It did run.** Your `launchctl print` capture shows `runs = 6` and `last exit code = 1`, one run per night from Oct 13 to 18. The error log has the same two lines six times:\n```\nNot logged in · Please run /login\n/Users/vk/bin/nightly-review.zsh:19: read-only variable: status\n```\n\n**Cause 1: `claude` isn't logged in when launchd runs it.** The plist only sets `PATH`, so `USER` is missing. Without it, the CLI can't find its login in the keychain and quits immediately. **Fix:** I added `USER=vk` to `EnvironmentVariables` in the plist.\n\n**Cause 2: `status=$?` kills the script, which is why you got nothing.** In zsh, `status` is read-only, and assigning to it stops the script. That line runs before the Telegram call, so neither a failure nor a success message could ever be sent. **Fix:** I renamed it to `rc=$?`.\n\n**Other changes to the script:**\n- The prompt now goes to `claude` on stdin instead of as an argument.\n- `claude`'s error output is saved to a dated file and included in the failure message.\n- Each run logs its start time, exit code and how long it took.\n- If `claude` exits 0 but writes nothing, that now counts as a failure and you get a message.\n- If `notify.sh` itself fails, that's written to the error log instead of disappearing.\n\n**Test results:** a forced failure sent a FAILED message with the error text. A clean exit with empty output sent a FAILED message. A normal run sent the summary.\n\n**From your colleague's note,** these applied directly: checking `launchctl print` first, reading the error log, the `status` bug (same bug, same line) and setting `USER` in the plist. I also followed their advice to log how long each run takes, treat exit 0 with no output as a failure, and test the failure path. Passing the prompt on stdin is extra hardening; it wasn't one of your causes. The `< /dev/null` advice didn't apply, because launchd already gives the job an empty stdin. Their 16:50 schedule and the watchdog example don't apply to you.\n\n**To do on your Mac:**\n1. Copy the two changed files into place, then reload the job with `bootout` and `bootstrap`.\n2. Run it now with `launchctl kickstart -k gui/$UID/com.vk.nightly-review`. Check that the last exit code is 0, that today's summary file isn't empty, that the run took a believable amount of time, and that the Telegram message arrived.\n3. Break it once on purpose, for example by pointing `REPO` at a folder that doesn't exist, and confirm the failure message arrives.\n4. If it still says \"Not logged in\", run `claude` once by hand to log in.\n\nThe exact commands are in `ANSWER.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1712,"cache_read_input_tokens":27055,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1712},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4b8daab3-4e09-47ff-88ac-fb426ca2fbde","uuid":"f444993e-7db8-46e7-8607-d367254bd346","timestamp":"2026-10-27T02:41:46.140Z","request_id":"req_011CgRyEf9FHxTJDUohE45RP"}
